WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
How do we measure success
in language learning?

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:07.770
I'll tell you how I don't measure
success in language learning, and that

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:14.760
is in getting, you know, nine out of 10
questions right on a test or a drill,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:20.370
because I know from experience that
I can get some things correct on one

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.470
occasion and get them wrong the next time.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.670
So it's not really, in my opinion,
a good measure of success.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:33.045
I have said many times that what we
like to measure at LingQ and what

00:00:33.495 --> 00:00:37.845
school language programs should
measure is the level of activity.

00:00:38.565 --> 00:00:42.165
Because if we stay active with
the language, we will improve.

00:00:42.195 --> 00:00:44.175
We cannot help but improve.

00:00:44.475 --> 00:00:49.365
And so at LingQ we measure, uh, you
know, hours of listening, words read,

00:00:49.665 --> 00:00:51.825
words looked up, which is LingQs created.

00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:54.135
And so we measure the level of activity.

00:00:54.135 --> 00:00:54.875
We have...

00:00:54.875 --> 00:00:57.045
we have a composite activity index.

00:00:57.075 --> 00:01:02.385
If you stay active, you will
improve because the, the brain

00:01:02.385 --> 00:01:03.675
is acquiring these words.

00:01:03.825 --> 00:01:06.975
You may feel that you're not
improving, but in fact you are.

00:01:07.245 --> 00:01:11.640
So from that perspective, success
to me in language learning

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.490
is are we staying active?

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.800
Are am I staying the course?

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.670
Am I spending time with the language,
whether on LingQ or whether I'm reading

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.460
a book on paper or talking to people?

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.590
Am I active with the language?

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.009
As long as I'm active with
the language, I'm successful.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.940
Uh, we can keep track of that
the way we do at LingQ or

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.410
you might wanna keep a diary.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.770
How many, you know, how much time
do I spend with the language?

00:01:38.115 --> 00:01:40.935
Um, you may just have that impression.

00:01:40.935 --> 00:01:43.634
It seems recently I've been reading
a lot in the language or I've been

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:44.955
watching movies in the language.

00:01:45.494 --> 00:01:49.065
As long as you are engaging with
the language, even though you

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:52.845
might feel you're on that plateau,
and I often get the question,

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.725
you know, I'm on the plateau, I
really don't think I'm improving.

00:01:56.235 --> 00:02:01.095
So you sort of have a negative, you
know, feeling about your degree of

00:02:01.095 --> 00:02:02.535
success in learning the language.

00:02:03.164 --> 00:02:09.315
As long as you are active, to me that is
success because I know, again, from my

00:02:09.315 --> 00:02:13.185
experience at LingQ that if I stay with
it, if I'm reading every day, if I'm

00:02:13.185 --> 00:02:17.655
creating LingQs, even though I may not
be deliberately learning anything, in

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.954
fact, my known word count is increasing.

00:02:21.585 --> 00:02:26.204
And I know from experience, if I am
listening, continuing to listen a lot,

00:02:26.204 --> 00:02:30.555
every day, the brain is becoming more
and more familiar with the language.

00:02:31.155 --> 00:02:35.445
Every opportunity I have to speak,
maybe with a tutor, I'm engaged

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.475
with the language I'm using,
the language that is success.

00:02:38.475 --> 00:02:42.945
The process is the reward I have
said before, but the process is

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:46.995
always, is also the point of success.

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:49.644
As long as you are engaged,
you are successful.

00:02:50.385 --> 00:02:55.965
How much you improve, how much you're able
to use, the words that you have learned

00:02:55.995 --> 00:02:58.245
is going to depend on a number of factors.

00:02:58.364 --> 00:03:00.285
It's going to depend on opportunities.

00:03:00.495 --> 00:03:04.755
It's gonna depend on, say the subject
matter of a discussion you have.

00:03:04.935 --> 00:03:05.445
It's going to...

00:03:05.625 --> 00:03:09.135
say in terms of how well you speak, it's
gonna depend on how well you connect

00:03:09.135 --> 00:03:10.156
with the person you're talking to.

00:03:10.161 --> 00:03:13.170
How well uh, you understand
the subject matter.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.790
Uh, there's so many things that can
impact that, but the one thing that

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:22.170
is objectively true is that the more
you are engaged with the language,

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:25.620
the more active you are with the
language, the better you will do.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:30.120
If you can force yourself, if you
can nudge yourself through, you

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.130
know, streaks at LingQ through.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:36.410
Having a discipline that you're
gonna have, you know this habit.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:39.560
I've mentioned Atomic Habits:
every morning I get up, first thing

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.450
I do, I listen to my language.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:46.370
If you can force yourself into a pattern
where you are regularly engaged in

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.090
language learning activities such as
listening, reading, speaking, if you

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.310
are doing that, you are successful.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:56.960
You cannot force the success, you cannot
force your progress in the language.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:02.505
You can only commit yourself or nudge
yourself or discipline yourself or create

00:04:02.505 --> 00:04:07.665
the habits, the habits of success, the
habits of being active with the language.

00:04:07.665 --> 00:04:13.755
So to me, the measurement of success in
the language is how active have I been?

00:04:13.815 --> 00:04:15.495
How active am I now?

00:04:15.765 --> 00:04:19.485
For example, I very much
enjoyed my visit to Poland.

00:04:19.784 --> 00:04:24.945
I've got both loaded on LingQ and in
traditional book form material about

00:04:24.945 --> 00:04:26.715
the history of Poland and a novel.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:32.280
And I'm just, I feel I'm very successful
because I'm engaging with this material.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:36.750
And I know that by engaging with
this material, my familiarity with

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:41.250
Polish, my comprehension of Polish,
I mean, I see it already now, I,

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:44.240
I, I read and I understand more and
more and more of what I'm reading.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:49.200
And so the success comes from being
actively engaged with the language.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.210
So how do we measure success?

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:56.625
We measure how active we are
with the learning process.

00:04:57.285 --> 00:04:58.965
Everything else will look after yourself.

00:04:59.775 --> 00:05:00.525
Thanks for listening.

00:05:00.615 --> 00:05:01.095
Bye for now.

